    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g3wyglq",
      "content": "The Chhattisgarh Police is governed by the Police Act and the state government's guidelines. The police force maintains law and order, investigates crimes, and performs various duties under the Code of Criminal Procedure (CrPC), Indian Penal Code (IPC), and other relevant laws."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "10mbf8v",
      "content": "Important: The Indian Penal Code (IPC) 1860 has been replaced by the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) 2023, Code of Criminal Procedure (CrPC) by Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS) 2023, and Indian Evidence Act by Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam (BSA) 2023. These new laws came into force from 1 July 2024 and are critical for SI exam preparation."
    },
